>
> You can easily price-ID ?oEW as the only other scroll for $60 is blank
> paper, which always appears as "unlabled". Scrolls for $80 can be either
> enchant armor or remove curse, which are both safe to read if non-cursed
> and you are not wearing any heavily enchanted pieces of armor. Scrolls
> for $100, $200, and $300 are in general not safe to read.

Because scrolls at 100, 200 and 300 are not safe the other prices are. 
That makes a number of the cheaper scrolls safe but leaves plenty that
are still dangerous.  So I'll read identify any that are priced below
100.

At 100 the dangerous ones are fire and destroy armor.  If you are
wearing a cursed piece of armor and nothing else subject to fire it may
be worth trying scrolls priced 100 in a closed room.  Once you know
those two the others are no longer dangerous by process of elimination.

At 200 the dangerous one is amnesia.  It's arguably the worst one to
learn by reading.  Learn it and the other 200 priced ones are safe by
process of elimination.

At 300 the dangerous one is punishment.  If you have a scroll of remove
curse available then it's safe to read any of them at that price to
identify them.  Or if you have a pet rock mole ;^)


